{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
  "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:07 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Given that the issue of subject matter jurisdiction appears not to be in dispute, the issues before the Court today are: First, the scope of section 10(b) of the 1934 Exchange Act when applied to alleged fraudulent conduct with respect to financial information that is to be sent to Australia for incorporation into the financial statements of the Respondent, National Australia Bank. And second, the reasonableness of the application of the statute under these circumstances and the norms of enforcement pursuant to the private cause of action or otherwise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The communication was done between Florida and -- and Australia, and the senior management of HomeSide in Florida created those numbers with the expectation and the knowledge that those would go into the financial statement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is a $1.75 billion writedown in a portfolio. You have a portfolio of $187 billion worth of mortgages sitting down in Jacksonville, Florida."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Those derivatives are not at issue here, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what U.S. investor was harmed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you -- do you want to finish?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "George T. Conway, III",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The judgment of the court of appeals should be affirmed for two reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "George T. Conway, III",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, Petitioners have identified nothing in the text of section 10(b) that overcomes the presumption against extraterritoriality or the Charming Betsy Rule. The statutes should thus be construed not to apply to transactions and shares of foreign issuers on foreign exchanges. Second, unlike the rights of action that this Court has addressed in other extraterritoriality cases, the section 10(b) right is purely implied."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what is your test for whether -- whether it's being applied internationally or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask you on that point: Supposing the class of plaintiffs included a group of Americans who were shareholders of the Australian bank and who -- but who purchased their stock over the Australian exchange."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would the limitations on discovery give you substantial protection were we to adopt the government's test or say the foreign exchange test with the subset exceptions for the -- that takes account of the government's test?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "George T. Conway, III",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We argued that Mr. Morrison's claims should be defeated on the grounds that he had no damages, which was an absolutely ironclad calculation best based on a -- on a provision of the PSLRA, and we also argued that all of the claims should be dismissed for failure to plead fraud with the requisite particularity of the PSLRA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, is that your only point? Or is your point also that you wouldn't need"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Matthew D. Roberts (United States)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bd9dfb09176-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In our view, the alleged fraud violated Section 10b, because significant conduct material to the fraud's success occurred in the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1191",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "2bd9dfb091769f040e7b3e13741339415f71e10692f51684716231fd2f30b6de",
